<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 1 June, from 193 to 1980.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/septimius-severus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">193 <span class="tih-ago">1,833 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Didius Julianus is killed as Severus nears Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abandoned by the Senate and the Praetorian Guard, Didius Julianus was killed in the palace after a reign of 66 days. Septimius Severus entered Rome soon afterwards and founded a new dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1495 <span class="tih-ago">531 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scottish exchequer records malt for 'aqua vitae'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An entry in the Exchequer Rolls records malt given to Friar John Cor 'to make aqua vitae' for King James IV. It is the earliest known written reference to whisky distilling in Scotland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1533 <span class="tih-ago">493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Boleyn is crowned Queen of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six months pregnant with the future Elizabeth I, Anne Boleyn was crowned in Westminster Abbey. Her marriage to Henry VIII had required England's break with the papacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1794 <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howe defeats the French fleet on the Glorious First of June</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lord Howe's Channel Fleet captured six French ships of the line far out in the Atlantic. Yet the grain convoy the French were protecting reached France safely.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1796 <span class="tih-ago">230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tennessee becomes the 16th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tennessee was the first state created from a federal territory, the Territory South of the River Ohio. It later produced three presidents: Andrew Jackson, James Polk and Andrew Johnson.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1812 <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Madison asks Congress for war with Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Madison's message cited the impressment of American sailors and British restrictions on neutral trade. Congress declared war on 18 June, beginning the War of 1812.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1813 <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Shannon captures USS Chesapeake off Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a fight lasting about fifteen minutes, HMS Shannon took the American frigate Chesapeake. The dying American captain James Lawrence's words, 'Don't give up the ship', became a US Navy motto.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1980 <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">CNN launches as the first 24-hour news channel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ted Turner's Cable News Network began broadcasting from Atlanta. Its round-the-clock coverage created the modern continuous news cycle.</p></div></li></ol>
